        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-129461",
        ":question/problem": "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 6$ matrix and $B$ is a  $2\\times 4$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $BA?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "There are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication, and $BA$ is a $2\\times 6$ matrix:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 6}={BA}_{2\\times 6}\n$$"
      },
