        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-70705",
        ":question/problem": "Suppose $U$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $V$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $VU?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "There are $2$ columns in $V$ and $2$ rows in $U.$ Since the number of columns in $V$ equals the number of rows in $U,$ the matrices $V$ and $U$ are conformable for multiplication, and $VU$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix:\n\n$$\n{V}_{5\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{U}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}={VU}_{5\\times 3}\n$$"
      },
